      "content": "but it's not just stress... it feels too specific. like, it’s not just a reaction to what i see on the screen, it's like i'm sensing the momentum shift a few seconds before the data even populates. i even looked at my wearable data and the spikes happen exactly when the order flow changes. if it's not scientifically documented yet, isn't that just because the tech is too new? there has to be some kind of bio-electrical feedback loop happening between human intuition and the sheer amount of data moving through the wires. can you help me look into how bio-feedback might actually connect to market volatility patterns?",
